    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.map\n\n### Description\n\nIs there a way to cause \"left\" alignment of mini.map to indent the primary buffer, or is this a bug? Included a screenshot for comparison of default (\"right\") and \"left\" side setting on window.\r\n\r\nHere is my nvim config in case you can't reproduce and it's a conflict with a different plugin. https://gist.github.com/junelva/fc1017ee4ea116d987f6abbcf38d3bb8\r\n\r\nI also think that during left alignment the scroll line would look better on the right. Is that possible?\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/2194619/b23c6e1a-c45b-4dd3-b3a8-5087be7d30d3)\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Configure mini.map window.side = \"left\".\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe map creates space for the primary text buffer and number columns.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe map overlays the number columns and primary text buffer.",
