            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\n> Is there a way to cause \"left\" alignment of mini.map to indent the primary buffer, or is this a bug?\r\n\r\nBoth left and right alignment are implemented using floating windows which are drawn on top of normal windows. Affecting normal windows in any way (like moving them to not be shown beneath the map window) is out of scope.\r\n\r\n> I also think that during left alignment the scroll line would look better on the right. Is that possible?\r\n\r\nIn theory it is possible to implement but, unfortunately, also outside of scope. The initial primary use case for left alignment is to temporarily move map window from right to see text beneath it. So doing any additional adjustments for text in the map window is too costly maintenance-wise for the intended use case.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
